From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:11:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libcxx: keep the host headers out of the sim build

The sim build only passes -nostdinc++, so the host C library headers
stay visible to libc++ and win over the NuttX ones in two places.

__mbstate_t.h picks glibc's bits/types/mbstate_t.h before NuttX's
wchar.h, and the two mbstate_t definitions conflict. Try include_next
<wchar.h> first.

random.cpp includes linux/random.h and sys/ioctl.h whenever they can be
found. The host copies use a four argument _IOC while NuttX defines it
with two, so the build fails with

  macro "_IOC" requires 4 arguments, but only 2 given

Include them only when __linux__ is defined.

Signed-off-by: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
---
 include/__mbstate_t.h | 4 ++--
 src/random.cpp        | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/__mbstate_t.h b/include/__mbstate_t.h
index c23ea7113c..18c6dc5e88 100644
--- a/include/__mbstate_t.h
+++ b/include/__mbstate_t.h
@@ -39,12 +39,12 @@
 #  define __NEED_mbstate_t
 #  include <bits/alltypes.h>
 #  undef __NEED_mbstate_t
+#elif __has_include_next(<wchar.h>)
+#  include_next <wchar.h> // use the C standard provider of mbstate_t if present
 #elif __has_include(<bits/types/mbstate_t.h>)
 #  include <bits/types/mbstate_t.h> // works on most Unixes
 #elif __has_include(<sys/_types/_mbstate_t.h>)
 #  include <sys/_types/_mbstate_t.h> // works on Darwin
-#elif __has_include_next(<wchar.h>)
-#  include_next <wchar.h> // use the C standard provider of mbstate_t if present
 #elif __has_include_next(<uchar.h>)
 #  include_next <uchar.h> // Try <uchar.h> in absence of <wchar.h> for mbstate_t
 #else
diff --git a/src/random.cpp b/src/random.cpp
index 5c6644811b..9fcc802208 100644
--- a/src/random.cpp
+++ b/src/random.cpp
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 #elif defined(_LIBCPP_USING_DEV_RANDOM)
 #  include <fcntl.h>
 #  include <unistd.h>
-#  if __has_include(<sys/ioctl.h>) && __has_include(<linux/random.h>)
+#  if __has_include(<sys/ioctl.h>) && __has_include(<linux/random.h>) && defined(__linux__)
 #    include <linux/random.h>
 #    include <sys/ioctl.h>
 #  endif
